Z||000000||loafer87gt||01-31-2000||11:28 AM||||I'm slamming my 87 GT. I need to find a company that sells drop spindles my car though. The only place iI have been able to find is Street Dreams, and they want $300 bucks for the set. Is this price in line? I called BellTech and they said they no longer make their spindles. Any info would be good. BTW, anyone got a picture of a medium red 87 GT lowered with the factory wheels? thanx guys||||reg||1
Z||000001||william_thorniii||01-31-2000||12:48 PM||||Loafer,<P>I remember hearing that there was another but cannot for the life of me find it.  Here is the information that I have heard on Street Dreams.  Supposedly the Street Dreams are the Bell Tech.  When Bell Tech decided to discontinue the product, Street Dreams bought rights to the design.  They are in the prototype stage and there is no definite date of availability.  This could all be heresay, but it is as I have heard it.  If you find out any solid information on these spindles, please let me know.  I have every intention of putting them on my 86 SE.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000002||TwisT||01-31-2000||01:43 PM||||Ryane Motorsports,  Fiero suspension leader.  All products tested and tuned,  gaurenteed quality.  Service second to none...<P> <A HREF="http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ryanemotorsports.com/</A><P>...Forgot to mention,  prices are steeper and a brake upgrade is involved.  Also,  Ryane's '84-'87 bump-steer kit is almost done.  You may want to check that out,  at least...  =) <P><p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 01-31-2000).]||||reg||1
